What the unit responds to, in plain terms:
1. Bulgarian (or Russian) words that contain the Cyrillic hard sign "ъ": strong on the
   "ъ" itself and on the letters that follow it inside the same word.
2. Go source code: once a document has shown a few Go markers (func, package, import,
   :=, return, err, .go), Go structure tokens such as tabs, "//", " {", "/pkg" and
   quotes give a weak response; the words "go", ".go", " func" give a stronger one
   wherever they appear.

Everything else is predicted as 0. The rule is written as a simple text pattern and it
explains only part of the variance: most of the largest spikes are Bulgarian word pieces
without ъ and Go import lines, which this rule does not capture.
"""
