"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:280 (layer-0 MLP down-projection, one rank-one piece).

What it does: it is a word detector for sex and gender vocabulary. It is strongly negative
on the token for "gender" (about -6) and "sex" (about -4 to -5), moderately negative on
sexuality words and on demographic or personal-attribute words (age, birth, race, ethnic,
pregnancy, spouse, and their translations), and near zero on almost everything else. Its
activation depends almost only on the current token, not on context, so a word list
explains most of it.

The program: a lookup over the current token, lower-cased and stripped of its leading
space. Its prediction is a graded value per concept, zero for all other tokens.

What the simple version misses: a long tail of weakly negative or weakly positive
tokens (medical and biographical words, Japanese and Russian vocabulary, spelling
look-alikes such as "lender" or "Endian"). A full per-token table would add that tail,
but it would not be a readable explanation.
